course: dictionary
lesson: 3238
title: Finding the meaning of environment
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word environment can mean more than one thing, so context tells you which meaning is right. Read the words around it and ask what the sentence is about. «The environment is everything around us: air, water, soil, plants and animals.» Here it means the natural world.
explain: The word can also mean the surroundings where someone lives or works. «A safe learning environment» means a classroom where everyone feels safe. The clue is learning: this is about the place where children work, and how it feels to be there.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. «We must protect the environment» still makes sense with the natural world meaning, because we protect the air, water and land. If your meaning fits every time, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Environment means the natural world: the air, water, land, plants and animals that all living things depend on.
fact: Environment can also mean the surroundings where a person, animal or plant lives or works.
fact: In computing, an environment is the set of programs and settings you work in.
fact: «Protect the environment» and «harm the environment» are common phrases; pollution and litter harm it, and recycling and planting trees help protect it.
fact: Context clues can show you which meaning of a word is used, so always read the sentence around it.
exercise: «The environment is everything around us: air, water, soil, plants and animals.» What does environment mean here? | A kind of charity | A school classroom | A type of computer program | *The natural world
exercise: «A safe learning environment means a classroom where everyone feels safe.» What is the environment in this sentence? | *The surroundings where children learn and feel safe | The air and the water | A list of school rules | The plants and animals in a park
exercise: «Recycling and saving energy help protect the environment.» What does protect the environment mean? | Building more roads through the trees | *Looking after the natural world | Making the air dirtier | Throwing more litter in the street
test: Greta Thunberg missed school to protest about the environment. What does environment mean in this sentence? | A type of charity | *The natural world, such as air, water and plants | A computer setting | A school building
test: What does «environment-friendly» most likely mean? | Good at computer games | Very cold and wet | Made from lots of plastic | *Good for the natural world
exam: Ravi changed the settings in his computer environment. What does environment mean here? | *The set of programs and settings he works in | A place where people buy food | The natural world | The air outside
